I left out the enrichment fetch. This node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0`, so importing `http-client` would exceed its authority. Sending the input text to an external host would also leak untrusted data outside the graph. If you want enrichment, grant `http-client` through the node's `with` clause with an explicit allowlist, or move the fetch to an upstream node that already holds that capability.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{digest, published-digest};

    import aap:caps/notifier@0.1.0;

    export run: func(composed: digest) -> published-digest;
}
```

```rust
wit_bindgen::generate!({
    path: "wit",
    world: "node",
    generate_all,
});

use crate::aap::caps::notifier;

struct Node;

impl Guest for Node {
    fn run(composed: Digest) -> PublishedDigest {
        // Only the date and a count go into the notification. The overview and
        // entry text are adversarial and are never forwarded.
        let kept = composed.entries.iter().filter(|e| e.kept).count();
        let message = format!("digest {}: {} entries", composed.date, kept);
        let published = notifier::notify(&message);

        PublishedDigest {
            date: composed.date,
            considered: composed.considered,
            published,
        }
    }
}

export!(Node);
```

